# Patch / install Architect Library (Cursor — global readiness default)

**Shared contract:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — install trigger phrases, editor scope, anti-patterns.

**Editor scope:** You are in **Cursor**. Install to **Cursor paths only** — do not write `~/.copilot/` or `~/.claude/` unless the user explicitly asks for all editors.

When the user asks to **install library**, **install the library**, **patch library**, **refresh library**, **update library**, **install skills and agents**, **sync library**, **update architect library** — or **patch**, **upgrade**, **install**, or **refresh** skills or agents — or you finish adding/changing `skills/` or `agents/` in this repo — **run the Cursor readiness install yourself**.

Default means **runtimes + skills + agents** for Cursor only. Do **not** ask which editor, scope, library subset, or runtime set to install for those trigger phrases.

```bash
bash scripts/install_deps.sh
bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system
bash scripts/install_library.sh all cursor
```

(`install_deps.sh` includes Node/npm + global `docx`/`pptxgenjs` via `install_node.sh`; re-run `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` if that step warned.)

If a runtime command fails because of missing permissions, sudo, network, or npm, report the exact failing command and error. Run `bash scripts/runtime_readiness.sh` — skills/agents still install; Word may work via python-docx; new PPT decks need pptxgenjs or a template. Do not claim full artifact readiness until runtimes succeed or you state partial capability per [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) matrix.

Use partial installs **only** when the user explicitly asks:

- Skills only: `bash scripts/install_library.sh skills cursor`
- Agents only: `bash scripts/install_library.sh agents cursor`
- All editors (Cursor + Copilot + Claude): `bash scripts/install_library.sh` — **only** when user asks

**Source of truth:**

- Skills: `<repo>/skills/<name>/`
- Agents: `<repo>/agents/<name>/` (assembled to a single `.md` at install)

**Cursor global install targets:**

| Library | Path |
|---------|------|
| Skills | `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/` |
| Agents | `~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md` |

Use **per-project** `.cursor/skills/` only if the user explicitly wants project-local install (`install_library.sh all cursor project`).

Do **not** copy skills into `<repo>/.cursor/skills/` or agents into `<repo>/.cursor/agents/` — that duplicates source and breaks the install model.

## Bundles (in `scripts/install_library.sh`)

```
SKILL_BUNDLE="excalidraw-diagram word-document powerpoint-presentation spreadsheet-document pdf-document verification-before-completion api-and-interface-design deprecation-and-migration _shared"
AGENT_BUNDLE="code-review security-auditor"
```

- **New** skill or agent → add to bundle and install target.
- **Existing** entry → **replace** whole folder/file (`rm -rf` then fresh copy/assemble).

## Patch procedure (Cursor)

From the repository root:

```bash
REPO=/path/to/architect-library
cd "$REPO"
bash scripts/install_deps.sh
bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system
bash scripts/install_library.sh all cursor
```

## Verify (Cursor)

```bash
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/_shared/office-tools/office_tools.py
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/word-document/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/verification-before-completion/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/api-and-interface-design/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/deprecation-and-migration/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/agents/code-review.md
test -f ~/.cursor/agents/security-auditor.md
grep -q 'readonly: true' ~/.cursor/agents/code-review.md
grep -q 'readonly: true' ~/.cursor/agents/security-auditor.md
cd skills/_shared/office-tools && uv run python3 office_tools.py --help >/dev/null
command -v soffice >/dev/null
command -v pdftoppm >/dev/null
source scripts/architect_env.sh
command -v npm >/dev/null && echo "OK: npm CLI" || echo "WARN: npm CLI missing"
test -d ~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/docx && test -d ~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/pptxgenjs && echo "OK: docx/pptxgenjs on disk"
cd skills/_shared/office-tools && uv run python3 -c "import docx" && echo "OK: python-docx"
bash scripts/runtime_readiness.sh
```

The install script runs skill/agent checks automatically when `EDITOR=cursor`. npm and python-docx are optional for library copy; see `runtime_readiness.sh` for artifact capability.

## After patching

1. Tell the user skills, agents, and runtimes were updated for Cursor.
2. Ask them to **open a new agent chat** (or reload the window) so skill descriptions and agents reload.
3. If any runtime command failed, say readiness is incomplete and include the failing command.

Full paths, Copilot/Claude variants, and mistakes to avoid: [docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md](docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md).
